                                  FOR

                               BRADIPO I







          Alessio Albertoni
          
              
                              




  Quote of the Week:

  John II, King of Poland, after routing the Turks from Vienna in 1683 A.D.:
  "The immortal God... has blest us with so signal a victory as scarce the 
memory of man can equal.  Thanks be to Heaven, now the Half-Moon triumphs no 
longer over the Cross!"


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:

  With the coming of the spring season Babba Sissoko (#0) prepared to quench 
his thirst for glory.  Bradipo I has been notified by Babba Sissoko that his 
cooperation has become expendable, and thus our formerly amicable relations 
are now broken.

  Stormy winter melted into sweet spring.  Bradipo I could not cast Flood on 
Transylvania because Mountain terrain is illegal for the Flood spell.  So, 
Bradipo I tried hard to improve his Tactics, but he practiced in vain.

  In Kiska, Bradipo I campaigned against the provincial Eagle chieftain.  
Bradipo I commanded the invading armies.  The defenders were led by the 
provincial Eagle chieftain.  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle 
as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Kiska (0207):

   32nd     290th   
  Lt Cav   Phalanx  
